WEBVTT

welcome-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
Hello Imran.

welcome-2
00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:05.000
This video helps you get ready for your colonoscopy at Brackenridge.

welcome-3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.923
It takes about two minutes.

welcome-4
00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:12.308
You can pause it, turn on captions, or ask a question at any time.

what-happens-1
00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:19.231
A thin, flexible tube with a camera is used to look at the lining of your large bowel.

what-happens-2
00:00:19.231 --> 00:00:22.692
You'll have medicine to make you relaxed and drowsy.

what-happens-3
00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:24.615
You won't be fully asleep.

what-happens-4
00:00:24.615 --> 00:00:29.231
It's a day case, so you should go home the same day.

when-where-1
00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:31.923
Your appointment is on Wednesday 4 November.

when-where-2
00:00:31.923 --> 00:00:33.462
Please arrive at 1pm.

when-where-3
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:37.308
Go to the Endoscopy Unit, Ground Floor, Brackenridge General Hospital.

when-where-4
00:00:37.308 --> 00:00:40.769
Expect to be with us for about 4 hours.

eating-drinking-1
00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:43.462
This part is important for your safety.

eating-drinking-2
00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:46.538
Don't eat anything after 9am the day before.

eating-drinking-3
00:00:46.538 --> 00:00:50.385
You can drink clear fluids until 11am on the day.

eating-drinking-4
00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:52.308
After that, nothing at all.

eating-drinking-5
00:00:52.308 --> 00:00:58.077
If you eat or drink after these times, we may have to cancel your procedure.

bowel-prep-1
00:00:58.077 --> 00:01:03.077
You'll need to take bowel preparation to empty your bowel before the test.

bowel-prep-2
00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:05.000
Follow the separate sheet exactly.

bowel-prep-3
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
It works quickly, so plan to stay at home, close to a toilet.

medicines-1
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.154
Now, your medicines.

medicines-2
00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:14.615
Stop taking iron tablets 7 days before your appointment.

medicines-3
00:01:14.615 --> 00:01:19.615
If you take blood-thinning medicines or medicines for diabetes, call the pre-assessment team.

medicines-4
00:01:19.615 --> 00:01:21.923
Do not stop them without advice.

what-to-bring-1
00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:28.846
Please bring a list of your medicines, a dressing gown and slippers and your bowel preparation instruction sheet.

what-to-bring-2
00:01:28.846 --> 00:01:31.154
Leave jewellery and valuables at home.

going-home-1
00:01:31.154 --> 00:01:37.692
You must have a responsible adult to take you home and stay with you for 24 hours.

going-home-2
00:01:37.692 --> 00:01:42.308
Do not drive, cycle or operate machinery for 24 hours after sedation.

going-home-3
00:01:42.308 --> 00:01:45.385
You may feel bloated for a few hours.

going-home-4
00:01:45.385 --> 00:01:48.846
Most people are back to normal the next day.

warning-signs-1
00:01:48.846 --> 00:01:59.615
After you get home, call us straight away if you have any of these: severe tummy pain; passing more than a small amount of blood; a high temperature.

contact-1
00:01:59.615 --> 00:02:07.308
If you have a question, type it in the box next to this video, or call us on 01632 960348.

contact-2
00:02:07.308 --> 00:02:09.615
Outside office hours, call 01632 960999.

contact-3
00:02:09.615 --> 00:02:12.308
We look forward to seeing you, Imran.
